}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c21086c0-3a9c-5573-ada7-1e60cd748d7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347029} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b81f0df-36b6-5fad-ad8a-f214b05bb9a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347796}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6a2f73e-e22a-577f-8047-7f3fcc20b4ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-79189" :question/problem "![](images/20/20c1f81e9737856b7cf1fbf031fd42988a37eb418303114d95f6521c0401fa61.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $2$ centered at $(4,-3)$, as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(6,-3)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +a,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +b,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the circle is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(r+a,b).$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $2$ centered at the point $(4,-3).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +4,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348170 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f11f8f5-14af-5418-a30f-2cdb361b260a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346029} {:answer/id #uuid "60d87398-f4f2-5513-9687-a427c1be6407" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346190} {:answer/id #uuid "6661a258-7ca8-5569-93ca-fc1dce78c2f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +5,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346245} {:answer/id #uuid "80d564fe-11e4-5e17-ae8d-364ca396dbfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -4,\\,y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346476} {:answer/id #uuid "d68fa614-0fdb-5265-9177-7d915486a0ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +5,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60d87398-f4f2-5513-9687-a427c1be6407" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346190} :answer-field/id #uuid "00426326-692f-5b6d-a52b-4521d86868ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347605}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c8948ed-478d-597d-8d84-3303f297f4dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-79192" :question/problem "![](images/6b/6b77b1b8a61b5ec7306fbc0b3d70618e7fdce2237bdcbfd017c23c01b80f2979.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $3$ centered at $(-4,5)$, as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(-1,5)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +a,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +b,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the circle is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(r+a,b).$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $3$ centered at the point $(-4,5).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +5,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399496 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "146d3b28-8e29-5eb2-9b1c-13a2a90ec385" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399498} {:answer/id #uuid "d4d5787b-b5bd-5b27-a033-31a126fb604a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399499} {:answer/id #uuid "ebd95806-d79f-5932-8502-3d798b511be9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399500} {:answer/id #uuid "c7286f56-415b-5975-9965-cac2f25bbe61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -1,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399501} {:answer/id #uuid "4df757e2-103b-56a4-a77e-0738b69bd499" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4d5787b-b5bd-5b27-a033-31a126fb604a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399499} :answer-field/id #uuid "05f37ecc-6d85-5118-a9aa-9f9f01af2578" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399497}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "656ebe17-b886-53ff-b069-a7253f396457" :question/math-academy-id "q-106049" :question/problem "![](images/21/2135f70f6703878d5f82d3524c890af08e194d7fdfbe92e97a5305d142f73779.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $2$ centered at $(2,1)$, as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(4,1)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +a,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +b,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the circle is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(r+a,b).$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $2$ centered at the point $(2,1).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399503 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f37153f-6b80-5708-b6a4-edebf7c3a823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399505} {:answer/id #uuid "d0b71958-0b7a-58d5-aa67-e69e50d38e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399506} {:answer/id #uuid "e501da01-42b8-58ee-9609-f73020f69f4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399507} {:answer/id #uuid "08a3ceb4-1e5e-5d85-b566-0b5a554e82e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399508} {:answer/id #uuid "08282cf0-c65d-5a51-98dd-3a937c9e9dc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08a3ceb4-1e5e-5d85-b566-0b5a554e82e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399508} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b61b62a-5e5d-5935-a620-97cbe92e0582" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399504}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c45d1161-cc6e-56e5-89da-543c3e758d02" :question/math-academy-id "q-106051" :question/problem "Which of the following parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate a circle of radius $3$ centered at the point $(-3,2)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +a,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +b,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $3$ centered at the point $(-3,2).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Circle Centered at a General Point"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087768 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087585 :question/id #uuid "16faff9a-9599-5b8c-85cd-132f3e3f4b92" :question/math-academy-id "e-6150" :question/problem "The circle below is centered at $C(2, 0)$ and the point $X(-1, 4)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle.\n\n![](images/ec/ec8cd56c5a957321de6867c329d53839a924f66714de9941ebb088081680cfbf.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2 + (y-b)^2 = r^2.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(2-(-1))}^{2}+{(0-4)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088209 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41966cdb-4ae0-5538-9bc6-e14f91d4170f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330531} {:answer/id #uuid "8cd5e9e5-1f75-55a3-a81f-00682c5cd0dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331201} {:answer/id #uuid "91982f68-5ef2-530b-998a-6c4d449f2b6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331244} {:answer/id #uuid "aa024009-c4d9-5a22-a9e5-fe96f4fb3494" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331458} {:answer/id #uuid "ccb27233-f2ce-5f96-b456-6c8d1e14e5c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41966cdb-4ae0-5538-9bc6-e14f91d4170f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330531} :answer-field/id #uuid "859e0875-e943-5c0a-9921-5b1a5dbe9076" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332435}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "51473619-1294-5307-bfc0-3377a609fc5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-54215" :question/problem "![](images/63/63102dc32e44d75681b95ca5570c737224d7fd887d7c86d2b5c7a1e41a26c9f3.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(4,-4)$ and the point $X(-4,2)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(4-(-4))}^{2}+{(-4-2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-4)^{2}+(y-(-4))^{2} & =(10)^{2} \\\\ (x-4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2} & =100\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088292 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9c351e4-8bd6-5e57-9b6f-32dc18b88bd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 1)^{2} + (y + 2)^{2} = 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086407} {:answer/id #uuid "ceb055af-6e86-5af2-9d4e-27f5372d988c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 1)^{2} + (y - 2)^{2} = 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086408} {:answer/id #uuid "0e091c04-e028-5876-b964-f681d5d46426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 1)^{2} + (y - 2)^{2} = \\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086409} {:answer/id #uuid "5b7da5f6-d41c-5640-809e-40b797691500" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 1)^{2} + (y + 2)^{2} = 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086410} {:answer/id #uuid "5cfb2715-4047-59fb-923f-fb6f02e15f87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 1)^{2} + (y + 2)^{2} = \\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086411}] :answer-field/id #uuid "737a60c6-d0a0-5ba1-836e-5c4dc48c0d4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086406}] :question/id #uuid "b799a937-531d-51f5-bb46-daea903429ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-72616" :question/problem "![](images/9e/9e905d98eafd51cd455811dc9b84fbca74f45dedb7fd7363e9dd97c953b3170a.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-1, 2)$ and the point $X(2, 3)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253304 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b0c7c14-a555-5e01-8838-765e944ceedf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250784} {:answer/id #uuid "78dc7686-f3de-5b7d-8046-a89585820e9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251556} {:answer/id #uuid "994030d6-5bdf-505c-ac30-a525c985caa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251870} {:answer/id #uuid "a7739a17-e686-57c5-ba6c-a87d9d4e8077" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251995} {:answer/id #uuid "d0408c11-e9e7-55cb-940f-15a1df96ac67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "994030d6-5bdf-505c-ac30-a525c985caa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251870} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0900e01-a03b-5ddb-af66-ba4873931f4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253187}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4be1d8bd-eb38-5bfc-b4eb-dd764bc3beed" :question/math-academy-id "q-117096" :question/problem "![](images/16/16d6786a4b1934ed234d4bf0896187aa6e93ec70cf045ddf4b743b1f51eaac2f.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-4,-3)$ and the point $X(-1,0)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{(-1-(-4))^{2}+(0-(-3))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={(3\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253305 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cb0ea5e-ad3e-596c-a47f-1b2f569400c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250794} {:answer/id #uuid "1dd34dda-6f93-5397-a33e-2a03884b982c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250807} {:answer/id #uuid "b690d28c-7840-5bec-9fea-01836e32189d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252161} {:answer/id #uuid "bff71f03-a6dd-5c42-a982-4c93c6ea8bd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252249} {:answer/id #uuid "dfbf80d1-3ee1-578b-9627-526049a9423e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b690d28c-7840-5bec-9fea-01836e32189d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252161} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d7781ff-a993-5178-9bac-63ccd91c2ea5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252969}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "014cf060-ee36-5cab-a46b-0c5421540a60" :question/math-academy-id "q-117099" :question/problem "![](images/2b/2bd7e3cb9594623c6f5dc3fad35c33c71df0efe9e80b2053dde33f4ef9080bda.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-4,-3)$ and the point $X(0,-1)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{(0-(-4))^{2}+(-1-(-3))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={(2\\sqrt{5})}^{2} \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341841 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27f70d2a-fc69-5d4c-8d76-eb29f542cee8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339477} {:answer/id #uuid "6d8195c7-e766-5e8a-9057-7cf807388cde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340095} {:answer/id #uuid "8aa99c96-03d0-5732-b316-93ca22442393" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340366} {:answer/id #uuid "c9082b17-653a-55a6-b4da-3fcc60887456" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340909} {:answer/id #uuid "e3377fdf-0433-59b7-872c-aa80d378fdc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27f70d2a-fc69-5d4c-8d76-eb29f542cee8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339477} :answer-field/id #uuid "30d50e00-9328-53c1-9634-e13ef473cc3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341463}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54aa38dd-d17e-53f7-9a6f-f5bb4a2cb026" :question/math-academy-id "q-72617" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d45a9c753270dfd9186bc16736d1815a11997c88d2f35a0c40f487e6acef66c6.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-2,3)$ and the point $X(1,-1)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(1-(-2))}^{2}+{(-1-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-2))^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341842 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "024d17a6-71d7-5b07-a9f7-4e90925b4266" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339148} {:answer/id #uuid "39733cc5-69a1-5e1d-bebb-7bb234749a05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339644} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc3778a-58ce-553d-acdf-2eca8ef39844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340954} {:answer/id #uuid "d77e9864-505e-5fbd-9ca7-87866b380248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341040} {:answer/id #uuid "e5fd184d-c4e9-5208-a605-04a08c3cfd8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5fd184d-c4e9-5208-a605-04a08c3cfd8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341162} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dcfaa52-1bc6-5a58-9c52-332c3dac793a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341630}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e9071118-1df3-5b01-93dc-2b5f04fcff39" :question/math-academy-id "q-72619" :question/problem "![](images/2f/2ff035f38f5892f61d1eb037c7e39c59c8ec5104babac45224c4902152a0cfaa.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-1,-3)$ and the point $X(1,1)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(1-(-1))}^{2}+{(1-(-3))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & =(\\sqrt{20})^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341843 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44ceba2e-461c-5d6f-94d0-fffabcaa7f4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339737} {:answer/id #uuid "67364410-21ff-5ab6-b499-984469e0f0b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340042} {:answer/id #uuid "7e6b7a0c-3051-526a-9636-efd77cb0b591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340268} {:answer/id #uuid "c00a31e7-30ad-5958-a723-a2568cb7ceb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340844} {:answer/id #uuid "ccdecbe3-6add-5929-86dd-7b81307f2bae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67364410-21ff-5ab6-b499-984469e0f0b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340042} :answer-field/id #uuid "59370454-96d7-5c69-8869-e408beefd110" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341537}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b538b794-53e2-55d6-941e-f772138f1dd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-72621" :question/problem "![](images/6e/6e68ede9db2528ea607fc6fd63f0ec4ca1c1378982239913ef49153e1cf5b609.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(3,-3)$ and the point $X(-1,2)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(-1-3)}^{2}+{(2-(-3))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{41}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & =(\\sqrt{41})^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =41\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087784 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087612 :question/id #uuid "4ffaeeac-95a0-598a-9880-166d03f810ce" :question/math-academy-id "e-6779" :question/problem "![](images/f4/f44fad12ad1f7d465423f92258caae38e0c536153ba2c3c3a6de573061c69993.png)\n\nThe quarter-circle above is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx = 6\\cos\\theta, \\qquad y = 6\\sin\\theta.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle  of radius $r$  centered at  the origin are\n\n$$\nx = r\\cos\\theta, \\quad y = r\\sin\\theta, \\quad \\theta \\in [0,2\\pi).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the radius $r = 6.$ So, the parametric equations of the *full* circle are \n\n$$\nx=6\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=6\\sin\\theta, \\quad \\theta \\in [0,2\\pi).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-circle, we associate the parameter $\\theta$ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the circle and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](images/4b/4bd384e2b1a9d0568617ddbfd5ac7dbe9630882b45c40d7912f4809a6e0be551.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta$ to $\\left[0,\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\right],$ we get the required quarter-circle.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the quarter-circle are \n\n$$\nx=6\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=6\\sin\\theta, \\quad \\theta \\in \\left[0,\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\right].\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d81c7ff-8459-5559-bfae-c2a9c3bc739e" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088362 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aa7d468-de7c-538e-9bba-c5e80bfff308" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345434} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e290fc-d418-57b7-a936-1d5bb9c090a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347037} {:answer/id #uuid "c3e73f0f-1975-59bc-be4d-1ebab1b85f95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347044} {:answer/id #uuid "c561f9d3-b982-54c5-9bf9-a1d1c261a046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347063} {:answer/id #uuid "cb9bc121-8232-58b0-9c4f-7d9f5b035ea2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\