ametric equations of the *full* circle are \n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in (0,2\\pi ].\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to the arc above, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the circle and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](images/3f/3f259a44786f9851588e212396f1c9fe3259a63c88b8c3090ebc6f1e50a6c456.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[\\pi ,2\\pi ]$, we get the required arc of the circle.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the arc of the circle are \n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [\\pi ,2\\pi ].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302098 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc3655a7-f8db-5846-af3c-25460c132af1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc3655a7-f8db-5846-af3c-25460c132af1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300983} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cf81aff-e496-5b8c-9552-7373708bbd68" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301321} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dc7372f-b6d1-5b9c-9751-ff4f797dc123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dc7372f-b6d1-5b9c-9751-ff4f797dc123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300514} :answer-field/id #uuid "daa2e725-2b7a-5a48-92ef-54503711ba85" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301929}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ea11e213-e469-58c8-9667-84ff5e30c91a" :question/math-academy-id "q-321947" :question