etric equations of a circle  of radius $r$  centered at  the origin are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the radius $r=6.$ So, the parametric equations of the *full* circle are \n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a semi-circle, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the circle and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](images/9f/9f515c8b70ee6902df4c694f7d7b50efb4ff54d24b0cb25b9173d439fea84210.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\pi ]$, we get the required semi-circle.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the semi-circle are \n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348186 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b94134f-ae73-5c60-b140-c0a778be3be9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346133} {:answer/id #uuid "86c958c2-3ce5-5ce6-989e-85615bed0ab3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346520} {:answer/id #uuid "87dfbbb3-8e02-53ab-9d43-bd679bba35b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346530} {:answer/id #uuid "95b7f520-e509-5e91-bac8-5146b1e4a855" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346660} {:answer/id #uuid "99e6e321-4fa5-51b5-b56f-5f1cf02d0ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99e6e321-4fa5-51b5-b56f-5f1cf02d0ffe" :answer/type {:db/ide