 \n\n$$\na+b+c=2+1+0=3.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299744 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ffc48ff-1011-56e8-978d-23ac82a79306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ffc48ff-1011-56e8-978d-23ac82a79306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297690} :answer-field/id #uuid "28ebc2c3-8f30-59dc-a757-e2f3006a8b32" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298775} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ab4fcc6-76c4-5164-a6f8-e99687699fd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ab4fcc6-76c4-5164-a6f8-e99687699fd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298155} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e857817-9ed7-5435-956e-848cd74bf5b0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299159} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfcfbf74-a02e-5cd5-884b-9d1f0073aa1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfcfbf74-a02e-5cd5-884b-9d1f0073aa1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298513} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5ed9190-0d64-5ee1-84d8-1118627244ad" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299469}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91c7e89c-c820-5a7a-92df-a70c7a4ed90d" :question/math-academy-id "q-319346" :question/problem "![](images/f5/f5297b339026b8b2ec9666a37bcb59a73297bf8a691690999ca41f5313cb3c93.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows train routes between three stations, where nodes represent the stations and arrows represent the directed lines between them. The (incomplete) route matrix below represents information about the number of routes between each of the three stations. Fill in the missing elements of the table.\n\n|  |  | To: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **A** | **B** | **C** |\n| From: | **A** | $0$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ |\n| **B** | {{field-2}} | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  |\n| **C** | $2$ | $0$ | $0$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our diagram.\n\n- There are $2$ arrows starting at Station A and ending at Station B. So, there are $2$ routes from A to B.\n\n- There is $1$ arrow starting at Station B and ending at Station A. So, there is $1$ route from B to A.\n\n- There are $3$ arrows starting at Station B and ending at Station C. So, there is $3$ route from B to C.\n\nTherefore, our route matrix is the following:\n\n|  |  | To: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **A** | **B** | **C** |\n| From: | **A** | $0$ | $2$ | $0$ |\n| **B** | $1$ | $0$ | $3$ |  |\n| **C** | $2$ | $0$ | $0$ |  |"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299755 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "688363d1-0681-5b00-b206-cc4adec9e75e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "688363d1-0681-5b00-b206-cc4adec9e75e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298000} :answer-field/id #uuid "12ec66a0-3e77-55f2-84c5-e378b3fad41c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298706} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9df090b-b672-53fd-a199-56606a3681a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9df090b-b672-53fd-a199-56606a3681a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 175921862986